  "script": "YouTube has no CarPlay app. But one free app puts your whole iPhone screen on your car's display, with no adapter box.\n\nOne screen on the way looks like a dead end. I'll get you past it.\n\nOpen the App Store and search CarTV. Install the one called CarTV, M3U IPTV Player and Cast.\n\nSwipe through the intro, and here's that screen: the Pro paywall. Close it. The free version still works. It just has a time limit, which Pro removes.\n\nNow connect your iPhone to CarPlay, and open CarTV on the car's display.\n\nThen pick up the iPhone, tap the Cast to Car tab at the bottom, and start mirroring.\n\nOpen YouTube, play anything, and it plays on the big screen. Because it mirrors the whole phone, it works with any app, even ones without a cast button.\n\nThis is for passengers, or for when you're parked. Never watch while driving.\n\nYou'll find the app link in the description and the pinned comment.",
